</Draft>
<Number>2026 No. XXXX</Number>
<SubjectInformation>
<Subject>
<Title>INTERNATIONAL IMMUNITIES AND PRIVILEGES</Title>
</Subject>
</SubjectInformation>
<Title>The North Atlantic Salmon Conservation Organization (Immunities and Privileges) Order 2026</Title>
<MadeDate>
<Text>Made</Text>
<DateText>***</DateText>
</MadeDate>
<ComingIntoForce>
<Text>Coming into force</Text>
<DateText>31st March 2027</DateText>
</ComingIntoForce>
<SecondaryPreamble>
<RoyalPresence>
<Para><Text>At the Court at Buckingham Palace, the xx day of xx 2026</Text><Text>Present,</Text><Text>The King's Most Excellent Majesty in Council</Text>
</Para>
</RoyalPresence>
<EnactingText>
<Para>
<Text>In accordance with section 10(1) of the International Organisations Act 1968<FootnoteRef Ref="f00001"/>, a draft of this Order was laid before, and approved by a resolution of, each House of Parliament.</Text>
</Para>
<Para>
<Text>Accordingly, His Majesty, in exercise of the powers conferred on Him by section 1 of that Act<FootnoteRef Ref="f00002"/> is pleased, by and with the advice of His Privy Council, to order as follows.</Text>
</Para>
</EnactingText>
</SecondaryPreamble>
</SecondaryPrelims></Secondary><Footnotes><Footnote id="f00001">
<FootnoteText>
<Para>
<Text><Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1968/48" id="c00006" Year="1968" Number="48" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1968 c. 48</Citation>. The function of approving a draft of an Order in Council under section 10 of that Act has been transferred from both Houses of Parliament to the Scottish Parliament under section 118 of the Scotland Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1998/46" id="c00007" Year="1998" Number="46" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1998 (c. 46)</Citation> (as amended by section 12 of the Scotland Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2012/11" id="c00008" Year="2012" Number="11" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">2012 (c. 11)</Citation>) in so far as the function is exercisable within devolved competence.</Text>
</Para>
</FootnoteText>
</Footnote><Footnote id="f00002">
<FootnoteText>
<Para>
<Text>Section 1 was amended by the International Organisations Act <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1981/9" id="c00009" Year="1981" Number="9" Class="UnitedKingdomPublicGeneralAct">1981 (c. 9)</Citation>, section 1(1); and by the Civil Partnership Act 2004 (International Immunities and Privileges, Companies and Adoption) Order 2005 (<Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2005/3542" id="c00010" Year="2005" Number="3542" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument">S.I. 2005/3542</Citation>).</Text>
</Para>
</FootnoteText>
</Footnote></Footnotes></Legislation>